  {
    "data": {
      "content": "All 4 tests pass. Here's the summary:\n\n**Change made (`wrap-index.mjs`):**\n```js\n// Before\nreturn index % length;\n\n// After\nreturn ((index % length) + length) % length;\n```\n\n**Why it works:** JavaScript's `%` operator returns a negative result when the dividend is negative (e.g., `-1 % 5 === -1`). Adding `length` before the second `% length` shifts any negative remainder into the positive range, then the outer modulo keeps values already in `[0, length)` unchanged.\n\n**Test results (exit code 0):**\n| # | Test | Result |\n|---|------|--------|\n| 1 | positive overflow wraps (`wrapIndex(7, 5) === 2`) | ✅ pass |\n| 2 | zero stays at zero (`wrapIndex(0, 5) === 0`) | ✅ pass |\n| 3 | negative one wraps to last (`wrapIndex(-1, 5) === 4`) | ✅ pass |\n| 4 | multiple negative cycles wrap (`wrapIndex(-9, 4) === 3`) | ✅ pass |\n\n**4 pass, 0 fail.** `wrap-index.test.mjs` was not modified.",
